<title>INDIA: India's Tata Tea 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India's Tata Tea 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    586.2     vs     460.8</p>
<p>    Income		6,994.4     vs   5,239.7</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	 6.5     vs	 6.0</p>
<p>    Other income	  180.0	vs    193.5</p>
<p>    Expenditure	 5,923.3	vs  4,464.6</p>
<p>    Interest		302.2	vs    173.4</p>
<p>    Depreciation	  122.7	vs     97.4</p>
<p>    Tax		     240.0	vs    237.0</p>
<p>Note: Tata Tea is among the largest tea makers in the world. The firm said its exports in 1996/97 (April-March) jumped 106 percent to 2.16 billion rupees compared to the year-ago period.</p>
<p>&quot;Tea prices tended to improve and stabilise towards the end of the year under review. Prices have since then registered a further increaes in the current financial year as a result of increased export demand and sustained domestic sales,&quot; Tata Tea said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
